    <statement><p>Approximate  <m>f_{x}(1,3)</m> using  the contour diagram of
<m>f(x, y)</m> shown below.</p>
<image xmlns:pi="http://pretextbook.org/2020/pretext/internal" pi:generated="webwork/images/Library__Michigan__Chap14Sec1__Q16__pg-image-1.png" width="50%"/>
<p><m>f_{x}(1,3) \approx</m> <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{12-10}{2.2}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>f_{x}</m>, we want to find a difference quotient
<m>f_{x} \approx \frac{f(x_0+h,y_0) - f(x_0,y_0)}{h}</m>.  Here, we have
<m>f(1,3) \approx 10</m>, and <m>f(3.2,3) \approx 12</m>.
Thus, we can take
<me>f_{x} \approx \frac{f(3.2,3) - f(1,3)}{2.2} =
    \frac{12 - 10}{2.2} = 0.909091.</me>




</solution>
